# Scheduled jobs for the Semester Dashboard.
#
# These go in ROOT's crontab, not Mason's. Install them with:
#
#   sudo crontab -e
#
# and paste the lines below the comments. docs/SETUP.md walks through this.
#
# WHY ROOT: the backup needs the encryption key and the Backblaze credentials,
# which live in a file only root can read (/etc/college-dashboard/env, mode 600,
# per SPEC §11). The script drops back to the database's own user before touching
# the database, so it never leaves root-owned files where the container writes.
#
# WHY CRON AND NOT THE APP: the backup has to keep running when the container is
# broken, which is exactly when last night's copy matters. Canvas polling, which
# only makes sense when the app is up, runs inside the app instead (M1).


# Nightly backup at 03:15 server time. Takes an online copy of the database,
# verifies it, encrypts it, copies it to Backblaze B2, and prunes old copies.
# Its outcome appears on the dashboard's status page either way.
15 3 * * * /home/mason/College-Dashboard/ops/backup.sh >> /var/log/dashboard-backup.log 2>&1


# Optional: keep the backup log from growing without limit. Trims it to its last
# 2000 lines on the first of each month. The log gains only a few lines a day, so
# this is tidiness rather than a real disk concern.
0 4 1 * * tail -n 2000 /var/log/dashboard-backup.log > /var/log/dashboard-backup.log.tmp && mv /var/log/dashboard-backup.log.tmp /var/log/dashboard-backup.log
